invariant: INV-16
file: p256_scalar.c
catches: test/docker-mips.sh
reason: mont_mul's inner product is the one place a secret scalar limb
  meets another, and ct_widemul is what keeps it four 16x16 pieces. This
  edit hands gcc the 32x32 product instead, so mips32r2 multiplies two
  whole limbs and the mips32r2-gcc-O2 spec reads far more than the two
  madd it records for this file
  (https://github.com/c4milo/chapulin/issues/122). The recorded two come
  from one constant-operand call and are 16 bits wide; this one is not,
  which is the difference the entry exists to hold. Only Ubuntu's mips
  gcc runs that spec, and the mips lane's container is where it runs
  locally. Its first step is lint-wide-multiply-gcc.
  The lane skips without docker, and this then reports unguarded rather
  than caught.

--- old
            uint64_t v = ct_widemul(a[i], b[j]) + t[j] + carry;
--- new
            uint64_t v = (uint64_t)a[i] * b[j] + t[j] + carry;
